<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct experiments to validate the theoretical lower bound on the minimal prompt length required for stable In-Context Learning (ICL). The experiments test the predictions of our theory across various datasets, encoders, and generators. Unless otherwise stated, we use deterministic decoding (e.g., temperature <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0</annotation></semantics></math> when supported) so that variability is dominated by demonstration resampling rather than token-level sampling noise. Full reproducibility specifications (prompt templates, demo selection/retrieval, representation extraction, decoding hyperparameters, random seeds, knee-point estimator, and confidence intervals) are provided in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Experimental Reproducibility Specification ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental setup</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a comprehensive experimental inventory to facilitate reproduction, ablation and future benchmarking:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets:</span> SST-2<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Socher et al., 2013</a>)</cite>, AGNews<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, Yahoo!Answers<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, TREC-6<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Voorhees and Harman, 1998</a>)</cite>, GSM8K<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, SVAMP<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Patel et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, HotpotQA<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2018</a>)</cite> and Natural Questions<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwiatkowski et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, covering sentiment, news topic, QA and multi-step reasoning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Encoders:</span> all-mpnet-base-v2, all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and paraphrase-MiniLM-L12-v2<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reimers and Gurevych, 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models:</span> Anthropic Claude-Sonnet-4-5, DeepSeek-Reasoner<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, Gemini-3-Flash-Preview, Kimi-k2-thinking<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, OpenAI gpt-5.2-chat-latest and Qwen-Max-Latest<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Numerical noise sensitivity of predicted prompt length <math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Lower CV indicates higher numerical robustness.</span></figcaption>
