<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_author">Z. Zhao, E. Wallace, S. Feng, D. Klein, and S. Singh</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_title">Calibrate before use: improving few-shot performance of language models</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_inbook">International conference on machine learning</span>,
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_pages">pp. 12697–12706</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#S1.p1.1" title="1 Introduction ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§1</span></a>.
</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Complete Theory Chain</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ICL prompt, randomness, and stability (formal).</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-shot prompt is formed from <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{K}:=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{K}:=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and a query input <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\mathrm{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\mathrm{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> via a fixed template <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Prompt}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗆𝗉𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Prompt}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Prompt}(S_{K},x_{\mathrm{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗆𝗉𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Prompt}(S_{K},x_{\mathrm{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the model induces an output distribution
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathsf{Prompt}(S_{K},x_{\mathrm{q}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝖯𝗋𝗈𝗆𝗉𝗍</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathsf{Prompt}(S_{K},x_{\mathrm{q}}))</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., over next tokens or over labels under a verbalizer).
The randomness we study comes from resampling (and, when relevant, reordering) the demonstrations in the prompt.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(ICL stability at <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a query input <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, a prompting template, the model parameters <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and a decoding rule
(e.g., greedy decoding with fixed temperature/top-<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>), so that the only randomness is induced by resampling
(and, when relevant, re-ordering) the demonstrations in the prompt.
Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be two independent sets of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations drawn i.i.d. from the same task distribution.
Define <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{K}:=\mathrm{Prompt}(S_{K},x_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Prompt</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{K}:=\mathrm{Prompt}(S_{K},x_{q})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{K}:=\mathrm{Prompt}(S^{\prime}_{K},x_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Prompt</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{K}:=\mathrm{Prompt}(S^{\prime}_{K},x_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>. ICL is stable at length <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> if</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\!\Big(d\big(p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid P_{K}),\;p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid P^{\prime}_{K})\big)\leq\tau\Big)\;\geq\;1-\xi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\Big(d\big(p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid P_{K}),\;p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid P^{\prime}_{K})\big)\leq\tau\Big)\;\geq\;1-\xi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a divergence between distributions (e.g., total variation, KL, or Jensen–Shannon).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Operationalization of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
In our direct stability measurements (Appendix <a href="#A12" title="Appendix L Direct Measurement of Distributional Stability (Definition 3.1) ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">L</span></a>), we instantiate <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> with
Jensen–Shannon divergence (JSD). For open-ended tasks, we evaluate distributions on a finite support given by
the union of the top-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> decoded candidates across seeds and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> values, with probabilities renormalized on this support.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Scope of the proxy and instantiation of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1 (ICL stability at (𝜏,𝜉)). ‣ 3.1 Problem setup and proxy objective ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> is stated for a general LLM output distribution.
Our theoretical analysis does <em id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> model the full LLM; instead it analyzes a computable spectral-coverage proxy under a frozen representation map <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and standard sub-Gaussian concentration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In black-box API settings, the generator typically does not expose hidden states; accordingly, in our experiments we instantiate <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=e(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=e(x)</annotation></semantics></math> using a fixed external encoder <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Encoders and representations ‣ Appendix C Experimental Reproducibility Specification ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>) and compute spectral quantities in the encoder space.
All non-asymptotic guarantees in Sections 3–4 pertain to this proxy.
When using the proxy to predict the generator’s ICL stability, we rely on an empirical proxy–generator alignment premise (validated in our experiments and optionally corrected via calibration) rather than claiming a first-principles equivalence between encoder geometry and the generator’s internal representations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, when we use the proxy to <em id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">predict</em> the generator’s ICL stability (Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1 (ICL stability at (𝜏,𝜉)). ‣ 3.1 Problem setup and proxy objective ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>),
we rely on an empirical proxy–generator alignment premise, rather than claiming a first-principles equivalence.
We validate this premise by direct distributional stability measurements and comparisons in Appendix <a href="#A12" title="Appendix L Direct Measurement of Distributional Stability (Definition 3.1) ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">L</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proxy objective (spectral coverage).</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Directly verifying Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1 (ICL stability at (𝜏,𝜉)). ‣ 3.1 Problem setup and proxy objective ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> is expensive because it requires repeated model queries under many resampled prompts.
We therefore study an observable sufficient condition based on the spectral coverage of demonstration representations.
Concretely, we form an empirical second-moment matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> from representations of the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations and require its spectrum to be bounded away from degeneracy.
Sections 3–4 provide non-asymptotic bounds and an observable two-stage estimator for this proxy, while later experiments validate that the proxy upper-bounds empirical knee-points and can be calibrated.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Assumptions</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze in-context learning under the following layered assumptions on the feature representation
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A1) Nominal assumption (strong).</span>
A deterministic feature map <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gaussian (e.g., <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi(x)\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi(x)\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>).
We work with the population <em id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">second-moment</em> matrix
<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma:=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\phi(x)\phi(x)^{\top}\right]\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma:=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\phi(x)\phi(x)^{\top}\right]\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
which does <em id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> require <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\phi(x)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\phi(x)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\phi(x)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\phi(x)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, this second moment coincides with the covariance.
This assumption is adopted for the main theorem, under which all proofs are rigorous.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A2) Bounded representation drift (independent, non-identical).</span> Across the <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in-context demonstrations, the representation may drift with the context index <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We model this as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi_{t}(x)=\phi(x)+\Delta_{t}(x),\,\,t=1,\dots,K," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(x)=\phi(x)+\Delta_{t}(x),\,\,t=1,\dots,K,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are drawn independently across <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and the drift term satisfies the uniform bound</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{t}(x)\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon\quad\text{for all }x\text{ and all }t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{t}(x)\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon\quad\text{for all }x\text{ and all }t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Define the (population) second-moment at position <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[\phi_{t}(x)\phi_{t}(x)^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[\phi_{t}(x)\phi_{t}(x)^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math> and its average <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{t=1}^{K}\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{t=1}^{K}\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our concentration analysis extends to this independent but non-identically distributed setting by applying matrix Bernstein to <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}-\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}-\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Robustness Extensions ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>), yielding the same functional form as (A1) but with an explicit <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent inflation of the variance proxy and an explicit bound relating <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> to the nominal <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A3) Moment relaxation.</span>
Instead of sub-Gaussian tails, we allow <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> to be sub-exponential or to satisfy bounded fourth-moment conditions.
Concentration results can be adapted with modified constants, leading to slightly larger sample-size requirements.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A4) Weak dependence.</span>
When the context induces dependence among features <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi_{t}(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi_{t}(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we assume a mixing or martingale-difference condition.
In this case, matrix concentration inequalities for dependent sequences apply, yielding bounds of the same form up to a dependence factor (Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Extensions to Dependent Features ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All formal proofs in the main text are carried out under the nominal assumption (A1).
The relaxed settings (A2)–(A4) are analyzed in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Extensions Beyond the Nominal Assumption ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, where we show that the main results remain valid up to controlled perturbation terms.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A frozen feature map <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is assumed, satisfying <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi(x)\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi(x)\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> (the vector <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm), without requiring <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\phi(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\phi(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">population second-moment</em> matrix is <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[\phi\phi^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[\phi\phi^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\phi]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\phi]=0</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with the covariance; otherwise it is the uncentered second moment. Let <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\operatorname{rank}(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\operatorname{rank}(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;d</annotation></semantics></math> we work on the support subspace), and denote the smallest nonzero eigenvalue by <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{r}(\Sigma)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{r}(\Sigma)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. For brevity we write <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)=\lambda_{r}(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)=\lambda_{r}(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A demonstration sequence <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{K}=\{x_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{K}=\{x_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of i.i.d. draws from <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{K}=\begin{bmatrix}\phi(x_{1})^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
\phi(x_{K})^{\top}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{K}=\begin{bmatrix}\phi(x_{1})^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
\phi(x_{K})^{\top}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}=\frac{1}{K}H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}X_{k},\\
X_{k}:=\phi(x_{k})\phi(x_{k})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}=\frac{1}{K}H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}X_{k},\\
X_{k}:=\phi(x_{k})\phi(x_{k})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robust proxy objective.</span>
For numerical robustness and to avoid excessive sensitivity to the extreme tail of the spectrum,
we consider two closely related spectral proxies.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(Ridge-regularized spectral floor).</em> Fix a small ridge level <math id="A1.I2.i4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and define the
regularized empirical second moment</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}\;:=\;\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}\;:=\;\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Our primary objective is to characterize the sample size <math id="A1.I2.i4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> needed for</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\big(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta\big)\geq 1-\xi," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\big(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta\big)\geq 1-\xi,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I2.i4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(\rho,\rho+\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(\rho,\rho+\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma))</annotation></semantics></math>.
This proxy is equivalent to requiring <math id="A1.I2.i4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta-\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta-\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, but is more stable
numerically and aligns with ridge/regularized linearized views of ICL.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I2.i4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(Quantile eigenvalue surrogate).</em> Alternatively, let <math id="A1.I2.i4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{(1)}(A)\leq\cdots\leq\lambda_{(d)}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{(1)}(A)\leq\cdots\leq\lambda_{(d)}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>
denote the eigenvalues of a PSD matrix <math id="A1.I2.i4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> in nondecreasing order, and define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}(A)\;:=\;\lambda_{(\lceil qd\rceil)}(A),\qquad q\in(0,1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}(A)\;:=\;\lambda_{(\lceil qd\rceil)}(A),\qquad q\in(0,1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">In practice we often use <math id="A1.I2.i4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="A1.I2.i4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in[0.05,0.2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in[0.05,0.2]</annotation></semantics></math>) to reduce over-conservativeness;
see Section <a href="#A1.SS7" title="A.7 Connection to ICL (in-context learning) and experimental suggestions ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a> for a lightweight calibration that preserves monotone dependence.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Basic matrix tail bound (a one-sided matrix Bernstein for the minimum eigenvalue)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}:=\phi(x_{k})\phi(x_{k})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}:=\phi(x_{k})\phi(x_{k})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and centered matrices <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{k}:=X_{k}-\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{k}:=X_{k}-\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}Y_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}Y_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\Sigma=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}Y_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\Sigma=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}Y_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Fix a ridge level <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and define the shifted population and empirical matrices</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\rho}:=\Sigma+\rho I_{d},\qquad\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}:=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\rho}:=\Sigma+\rho I_{d},\qquad\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}:=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}-\Sigma_{\rho}=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}-\Sigma_{\rho}=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
We aim to control <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})=\lambda_{\min}\!\Big(\Sigma_{\rho}+\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}Y_{k}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})=\lambda_{\min}\!\Big(\Sigma_{\rho}+\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}Y_{k}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By a matrix Bernstein inequality (a one-sided lower-tail form), there exist constants <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\Big(\lambda_{\min}\Big(\sum_{k=1}^{K}Y_{k}\Big)\leq-t\Big)\leq r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\Big(-\frac{t^{2}}{2v+\tfrac{2}{3}Rt}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\Big(\lambda_{\min}\Big(\sum_{k=1}^{K}Y_{k}\Big)\leq-t\Big)\leq r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\Big(-\frac{t^{2}}{2v+\tfrac{2}{3}Rt}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we take the effective-rank prefactor</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{eff}}:=\frac{\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)}{\|\Sigma\|}\leq\mathrm{rank}(\Sigma)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{eff}}:=\frac{\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)}{\|\Sigma\|}\leq\mathrm{rank}(\Sigma),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\Big\|\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}[Y_{k}^{2}]\Big\|=K\cdot\big\|\mathbb{E}[(X-\Sigma)^{2}]\big\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\Big\|\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}[Y_{k}^{2}]\Big\|=K\cdot\big\|\mathbb{E}[(X-\Sigma)^{2}]\big\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is (on a high-probability event) an upper bound for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k}\|Y_{k}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k}\|Y_{k}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rho}:=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma_{\rho})-\delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho-\delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rho}:=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma_{\rho})-\delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho-\delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and assume <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rho}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rho}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Setting <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=K\Delta_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=K\Delta_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ A.1 Basic matrix tail bound (a one-sided matrix Bernstein for the minimum eigenvalue) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\big(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\leq\delta\big)\leq r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\Big(-\frac{K\Delta_{\rho}^{2}}{2\widetilde{v}+\tfrac{2}{3}R\Delta_{\rho}}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\big(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\leq\delta\big)\leq r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\Big(-\frac{K\Delta_{\rho}^{2}}{2\widetilde{v}+\tfrac{2}{3}R\Delta_{\rho}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{v}:=\big\|\mathbb{E}[(X-\Sigma)^{2}]\big\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{v}:=\big\|\mathbb{E}[(X-\Sigma)^{2}]\big\|</annotation></semantics></math>; the detailed derivation is in the appendix.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Controlling <math id="A1.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R,\widetilde{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R,\widetilde{v}</annotation></semantics></math> under the sub-Gaussian assumption (truncation and fourth-moment bounds)</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Fourth-moment bound</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the vector <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> assumption <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> there exists an absolute constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|X\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\phi\phi^{\top}\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|X\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\phi\phi^{\top}\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">A noncommutative square inequality.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any symmetric matrices <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A-B)^{2}\preceq 2A^{2}+2B^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A-B)^{2}\preceq 2A^{2}+2B^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Indeed, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A+B)^{2}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A+B)^{2}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB+BA\succeq-(A^{2}+B^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB+BA\succeq-(A^{2}+B^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A-B)^{2}=A^{2}+B^{2}-(AB+BA)\preceq A^{2}+B^{2}+(A^{2}+B^{2})=2A^{2}+2B^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A-B)^{2}=A^{2}+B^{2}-(AB+BA)\preceq A^{2}+B^{2}+(A^{2}+B^{2})=2A^{2}+2B^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Applying (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ A noncommutative square inequality. ‣ A.2.1 Fourth-moment bound ‣ A.2 Controlling 𝑅,𝑣̃ under the sub-Gaussian assumption (truncation and fourth-moment bounds) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, and using
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}[M]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\mathbb{E}\|M\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}[M]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\mathbb{E}\|M\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{v}=\big\|\mathbb{E}[(X-\Sigma)^{2}]\big\|\leq 2\,\big\|\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]\big\|+2\|\Sigma^{2}\|\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}\|X^{2}\|+2\|\Sigma\|^{2}=2\,\mathbb{E}\|X\|^{2}+2\|\Sigma\|^{2}\leq 2C_{1}\sigma^{4}+2\|\Sigma\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{v}=\big\|\mathbb{E}[(X-\Sigma)^{2}]\big\|\leq 2\,\big\|\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]\big\|+2\|\Sigma^{2}\|\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}\|X^{2}\|+2\|\Sigma\|^{2}=2\,\mathbb{E}\|X\|^{2}+2\|\Sigma\|^{2}\leq 2C_{1}\sigma^{4}+2\|\Sigma\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Truncation to control R</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Typically <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X_{k}\|=\|\phi(x_{k})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X_{k}\|=\|\phi(x_{k})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is not almost surely bounded, but the sub-Gaussian tail implies that there exists an absolute constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathrm{tail}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathrm{tail}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\|\phi\|_{2}\geq t)\leq 2\exp\!\Big(-\frac{c_{\mathrm{tail}}\,t^{2}}{\sigma^{2}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\|\phi\|_{2}\geq t)\leq 2\exp\!\Big(-\frac{c_{\mathrm{tail}}\,t^{2}}{\sigma^{2}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Choose the truncation threshold</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{0}\;:=\;\frac{\sigma}{\sqrt{c_{\mathrm{tail}}}}\sqrt{\log\frac{8K}{\xi}}\;=\;:C_{2}\,\sigma\sqrt{\log\frac{8K}{\xi}},\qquad\text{where }C_{2}:=c_{\mathrm{tail}}^{-1/2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mi>σ</mi><msqrt><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>σ</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>where </mtext><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>tail</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\;:=\;\frac{\sigma}{\sqrt{c_{\mathrm{tail}}}}\sqrt{\log\frac{8K}{\xi}}\;=\;:C_{2}\,\sigma\sqrt{\log\frac{8K}{\xi}},\qquad\text{where }C_{2}:=c_{\mathrm{tail}}^{-1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then, for a single sample,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\|\phi\|_{2}&gt;t_{0})\leq 2\exp\!\Big(-\log\frac{8K}{\xi}\Big)=\frac{\xi}{4K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\|\phi\|_{2}&gt;t_{0})\leq 2\exp\!\Big(-\log\frac{8K}{\xi}\Big)=\frac{\xi}{4K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">By a union bound over the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> samples, with probability at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\xi/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\xi/4</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{1\leq k\leq K}\|X_{k}\|=\max_{k}\|\phi(x_{k})\|^{2}\leq B_{K}:=C_{2}^{2}\sigma^{2}\log\frac{8K}{\xi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{1\leq k\leq K}\|X_{k}\|=\max_{k}\|\phi(x_{k})\|^{2}\leq B_{K}:=C_{2}^{2}\sigma^{2}\log\frac{8K}{\xi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">On this high-probability event we may take</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\|X_{k}-\Sigma\|\leq B_{K}+\|\Sigma\|\leq C_{2}^{2}\sigma^{2}\log\frac{8K}{\xi}+\|\Sigma\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\|X_{k}-\Sigma\|\leq B_{K}+\|\Sigma\|\leq C_{2}^{2}\sigma^{2}\log\frac{8K}{\xi}+\|\Sigma\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Substitute into (<a href="#A1.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ A.1 Basic matrix tail bound (a one-sided matrix Bernstein for the minimum eigenvalue) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) to obtain a sample-size lower bound (one main result)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting (<a href="#A1.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ A noncommutative square inequality. ‣ A.2.1 Fourth-moment bound ‣ A.2 Controlling 𝑅,𝑣̃ under the sub-Gaussian assumption (truncation and fourth-moment bounds) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ A.2.2 Truncation to control R ‣ A.2 Controlling 𝑅,𝑣̃ under the sub-Gaussian assumption (truncation and fourth-moment bounds) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) into (<a href="#A1.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ A.1 Basic matrix tail bound (a one-sided matrix Bernstein for the minimum eigenvalue) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), and treating the rank-related prefactor <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a logarithmic factor, require the RHS to be <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\xi-\xi/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\xi-\xi/4</annotation></semantics></math>. One obtains a sufficient sample-size lower bound:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rho}=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho)=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho-\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rho}=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho)=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho-\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. If</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq\left[\frac{2\widetilde{v}}{\Delta^{2}}+\frac{2R}{3\Delta}\right]\log\frac{4r_{\mathrm{eff}}}{3\xi}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq\left[\frac{2\widetilde{v}}{\Delta^{2}}+\frac{2R}{3\Delta}\right]\log\frac{4r_{\mathrm{eff}}}{3\xi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">then (combining the truncation failure <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi/4</annotation></semantics></math> and Bernstein failure) we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta)\geq 1-\xi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta)\geq 1-\xi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Replacing <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> by the bounds from (<a href="#A1.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ A noncommutative square inequality. ‣ A.2.1 Fourth-moment bound ‣ A.2 Controlling 𝑅,𝑣̃ under the sub-Gaussian assumption (truncation and fourth-moment bounds) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ A.2.2 Truncation to control R ‣ A.2 Controlling 𝑅,𝑣̃ under the sub-Gaussian assumption (truncation and fourth-moment bounds) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) gives the explicit bound</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\gtrsim\left[\frac{2(2C_{1}\sigma^{4}+2\|\Sigma\|^{2})}{\Delta^{2}}+\frac{2\big(C_{2}^{2}\sigma^{2}\log(8K/\xi)+\|\Sigma\|\big)}{3\Delta}\right]\log\frac{4r_{\mathrm{eff}}}{3\xi}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\gtrsim\left[\frac{2(2C_{1}\sigma^{4}+2\|\Sigma\|^{2})}{\Delta^{2}}+\frac{2\big(C_{2}^{2}\sigma^{2}\log(8K/\xi)+\|\Sigma\|\big)}{3\Delta}\right]\log\frac{4r_{\mathrm{eff}}}{3\xi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where “<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gtrsim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gtrsim</annotation></semantics></math>” hides absolute constants and note <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> appears inside the <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(8K/\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(8K/\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> factor (a self-consistency issue); in practice one can use a single fixed-point iteration or replace <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(8K/\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(8K/\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> by the conservative upper bound <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(8K_{\max}/\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(8K_{\max}/\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>A more concise, commonly used operator-norm concentration (avoid truncation and the self-consistency)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the higher-level literature one often uses the following operator-norm concentration (Vershynin / Koltchinskii–Lounici style): there exists a constant <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for a sub-Gaussian vector</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\Big(\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\Sigma\|\geq C\|\Sigma\|\Big(\sqrt{\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}\Big)\Big)\leq\xi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\Big(\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\Sigma\|\geq C\|\Sigma\|\Big(\sqrt{\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}\Big)\Big)\leq\xi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#A1.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ A.4 A more concise, commonly used operator-norm concentration (avoid truncation and the self-consistency) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) to ensure <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (appendix explains why this suffices) we require</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\|\Sigma\|\Big(\sqrt{\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}\Big)\leq\Delta_{\rho}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\|\Sigma\|\Big(\sqrt{\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}\Big)\leq\Delta_{\rho}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Ignoring the lower-order <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{K}</annotation></semantics></math> term (negligible when <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is large), we get the simpler leading sample-size term:</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq C^{\prime}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{\Delta_{\rho}^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq C^{\prime}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{\Delta_{\rho}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant (<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}=C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}=C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>). This is the common practical form.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>A two-stage observable (plug-in) scheme and finite-sample guarantee</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bounds in (<a href="#A1.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ A.3 Substitute into () to obtain a sample-size lower bound (one main result) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ A.4 A more concise, commonly used operator-norm concentration (avoid truncation and the self-consistency) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) depend on unknowns <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma),\|\Sigma\|,r_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma,\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma),\|\Sigma\|,r_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now give an observable two-stage scheme and show it works in finite samples.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We implement the proxy using a small ridge level <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> to stabilize eigenvalue computations.
Throughout the theory, <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary scalar that is treated as fixed when applying concentration bounds
(i.e., the regularized matrices are <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\rho}=\Sigma+\rho I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\rho}=\Sigma+\rho I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In our implementation, we choose <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> in a scale-aware manner from the first-stage pilot sample and then hold it fixed:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\;:=\;\min\!\left\{\epsilon_{\rho}\cdot\frac{\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})}{d},\;\frac{\delta}{2}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\;:=\;\min\!\left\{\epsilon_{\rho}\cdot\frac{\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})}{d},\;\frac{\delta}{2}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}=10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}=10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> in float64 and <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}=10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}=10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> in float32.
The cap <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\leq\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\leq\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math> ensures <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, which avoids degeneracy in the spectral-floor condition.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Two-stage algorithm (high level)</h5>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Draw <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> samples (with <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> chosen theoretically below), compute <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> and calculate</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\lambda}_{0}:=\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho}),\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge}:=\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|,\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}:=\frac{\operatorname{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})}{\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\lambda}_{0}:=\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho}),\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge}:=\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|,\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}:=\frac{\operatorname{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})}{\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using the operator-norm deviation bound (<a href="#A1.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ A.4 A more concise, commonly used operator-norm concentration (avoid truncation and the self-consistency) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) (with <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> plugged in) construct a lower-confidence bound</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:=\widehat{\lambda}_{0}-C\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge}\Big(\sqrt{\frac{\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi_{j})}{K_{0}}}+\frac{\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi_{j})}{K_{0}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:=\widehat{\lambda}_{0}-C\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge}\Big(\sqrt{\frac{\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi_{j})}{K_{0}}}+\frac{\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi_{j})}{K_{0}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here we allocate a geometric failure budget: at iteration <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0,1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0,1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{j}:=\xi/2^{j+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{j}:=\xi/2^{j+2}</annotation></semantics></math> and invoke (<a href="#A1.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ A.4 A more concise, commonly used operator-norm concentration (avoid truncation and the self-consistency) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) with failure probability <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\geq 0}\xi_{j}\leq\xi/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\geq 0}\xi_{j}\leq\xi/2</annotation></semantics></math>. We reserve the remaining <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi/2</annotation></semantics></math> for the single second-stage bound.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, increase <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. double it) and repeat until <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> set <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}:=\lambda-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}:=\lambda-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> was chosen too large), and then use (<a href="#A1.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ A.4 A more concise, commonly used operator-norm concentration (avoid truncation and the self-consistency) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) with <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma\|,\ r_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma\|,\ r_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge},\ \widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge},\ \widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> to compute the second-stage sample size <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\;=\;C^{\prime}\,\frac{\widehat{\|\Sigma\|}^{2}\,\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{\widehat{\Delta}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\;=\;C^{\prime}\,\frac{\widehat{\|\Sigma\|}^{2}\,\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{\widehat{\Delta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The final total sample size is <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}+K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}+K</annotation></semantics></math>, and with total failure probability <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\xi</annotation></semantics></math> one guarantees <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Failure-probability accounting.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stage 1 uses a geometric allocation <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi_{j}\}_{j\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi_{j}\}_{j\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\geq 0}\xi_{j}\leq\xi/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\geq 0}\xi_{j}\leq\xi/2</annotation></semantics></math>, hence by a union bound all Stage 1 deviation
events used by the stopping iteration hold simultaneously with probability at least <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\xi/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\xi/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Stage 2 is executed once with failure probability <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi/2</annotation></semantics></math>, which is why the second-stage sample-size expressions use <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(4/\xi)=\log(2/(\xi/2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(4/\xi)=\log(2/(\xi/2))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore the overall two-stage procedure fails with probability at most <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Finite-sample correctness (theoretical guarantee)</h5>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#A1.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ A.4 A more concise, commonly used operator-norm concentration (avoid truncation and the self-consistency) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) for the first stage: if <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\|\Sigma\|\Big(\sqrt{\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}\Big)\leq\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\|\Sigma\|\Big(\sqrt{\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}}+\frac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}\Big)\leq\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">then with probability at least <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\xi/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\xi/2</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}-\Sigma\|\leq\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4},\qquad\big|\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|-\|\Sigma\|\big|\leq\frac{\|\Sigma\|}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}-\Sigma\|\leq\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4},\qquad\big|\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|-\|\Sigma\|\big|\leq\frac{\|\Sigma\|}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and, by Weyl’s inequality applied to <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho}=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}+\rho I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho}=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}+\rho I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\widehat{\lambda}_{0}-(\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho)\big|=\big|\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho})-\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma_{\rho})\big|\leq\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}-\Sigma\|\leq\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\widehat{\lambda}_{0}-(\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho)\big|=\big|\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho})-\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma_{\rho})\big|\leq\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}-\Sigma\|\leq\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|-\|\Sigma\|\big|\leq\|\Sigma\|/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|-\|\Sigma\|\big|\leq\|\Sigma\|/4</annotation></semantics></math> implies
<math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|\leq\tfrac{5}{4}\|\Sigma\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|\leq\tfrac{5}{4}\|\Sigma\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore the penalty term used in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Two-stage algorithm (high level) ‣ A.5 A two-stage observable (plug-in) scheme and finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) is at most</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\,\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|\!\left(\sqrt{\tfrac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}}+\tfrac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}\right)\leq\frac{5}{4}\cdot\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4}=\frac{5\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{16}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\,\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|\!\left(\sqrt{\tfrac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}}+\tfrac{r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{K_{0}}\right)\leq\frac{5}{4}\cdot\frac{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{4}=\frac{5\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{16},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">whenever (<a href="#A1.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Finite-sample correctness (theoretical guarantee) ‣ A.5 A two-stage observable (plug-in) scheme and finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) holds.
Combining this with <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\lambda}_{0}\geq\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho-\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\lambda}_{0}\geq\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)+\rho-\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)/4</annotation></semantics></math>
yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\;\geq\;\widehat{\lambda}_{0}-\frac{5\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{16}\;\geq\;\frac{7\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{16}+\rho." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\;\geq\;\widehat{\lambda}_{0}-\frac{5\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{16}\;\geq\;\frac{7\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)}{16}+\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">when <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> meets (<a href="#A1.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Finite-sample correctness (theoretical guarantee) ‣ A.5 A two-stage observable (plug-in) scheme and finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>). Thus there exists a constant <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime\prime}=16C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime\prime}=16C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) such that (<a href="#A1.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Finite-sample correctness (theoretical guarantee) ‣ A.5 A two-stage observable (plug-in) scheme and finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) is equivalent to the requirement</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}\geq C^{\prime\prime}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}\geq C^{\prime\prime}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Final implementable theorem statement</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[ICL Minimal Necessary Length, non-asymptotic, observable two-stage implementation]</span> Under the above setup, let <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(\rho,\rho+\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(\rho,\rho+\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma))</annotation></semantics></math> and failure tolerance <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. There exist absolute constants <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},C_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},C_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (depending on matrix-Bernstein and sub-Gaussian constants) such that:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Non-observable bound using spectral quantities)</span> If <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq C_{1}\Big(\frac{\sigma^{4}+\|\Sigma\|^{2}}{\Delta^{2}}+\frac{\sigma^{2}\log(8K/\xi)+\|\Sigma\|}{\Delta}\Big)\log\frac{4r_{\mathrm{eff}}}{3\xi}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq C_{1}\Big(\frac{\sigma^{4}+\|\Sigma\|^{2}}{\Delta^{2}}+\frac{\sigma^{2}\log(8K/\xi)+\|\Sigma\|}{\Delta}\Big)\log\frac{4r_{\mathrm{eff}}}{3\xi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">then <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta)\geq 1-\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta)\geq 1-\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. Ignoring lower-order terms (and using the sharper operator-norm concentration) yields the simplified dominant form</p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq C_{2}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{\big(\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho)\big)^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq C_{2}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(2/\xi)}{\big(\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-(\delta-\rho)\big)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which suffices in practice.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Two-stage observable implementation)</span> If the first-stage sample size <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}\geq C_{3}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}\geq C_{3}\frac{\|\Sigma\|^{2}r_{\mathrm{eff}}\log(4/\xi)}{\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">then forming <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> and constructing the lower confidence bound <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A1.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Two-stage algorithm (high level) ‣ A.5 A two-stage observable (plug-in) scheme and finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), and then setting <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}=\lambda-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}=\lambda-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and choosing <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> according to the rule in item (1) (with plug-in estimates <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge},\ \widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma\|_{\wedge},\ \widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>) yields, with total failure probability <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, the guarantee <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}+K,\rho})\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}+K,\rho})\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Connection to ICL (in-context learning) and experimental suggestions</h3>

<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">A one-shot practical calibration (heuristic; no formal guarantee).</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To tighten <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in practice, we use a calibrated proxy that preserves the same monotone dependence on spectral coverage
but replaces several conservative quantities by empirically better-behaved surrogates:
(i) replace <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma\|</annotation></semantics></math> by the Frobenius norm <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(ii) use the trace-based effective rank
<math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{tr}}:=\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)^{2}/\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi><mi>tr</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{tr}}:=\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)^{2}/\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(iii) replace the minimum eigenvalue by a low-quantile eigenvalue <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in[0.05,0.2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in[0.05,0.2]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid circularity, all spectral quantities in the calibrated proxy are computed from the <em id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">first-stage pilot matrix</em>
<math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (and its ridge-shifted version <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Define the unscaled calibrated prediction</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}(K_{0};q)\;:=\;\frac{\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{\,2}\;\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{tr}}\;\log(2/\xi)}{\big(\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho})-\delta\big)^{2}},\qquad\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{tr}}:=\frac{\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})^{2}}{\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{\,2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>raw</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi><mi>tr</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>eff</mi><mi>tr</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}(K_{0};q)\;:=\;\frac{\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{\,2}\;\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{tr}}\;\log(2/\xi)}{\big(\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho})-\delta\big)^{2}},\qquad\widehat{r}_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{tr}}:=\frac{\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})^{2}}{\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{\,2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We then apply a single global scale factor <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\mathrm{cal}}\;:=\;\left\lceil\alpha\cdot\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}(K_{0};q)\right\rceil." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>cal</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>raw</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\mathrm{cal}}\;:=\;\left\lceil\alpha\cdot\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}(K_{0};q)\right\rceil.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">How <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is determined from measured performance.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each encoder–generator pair, we choose a small calibration subset of tasks <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>cal</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>
(disjoint from the final evaluation tasks; Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Experimental Reproducibility Specification ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>).
For each task <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>cal</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we estimate an empirical knee-point <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>knee</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>
from the accuracy–vs.–<math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> curve, and compute <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}:=\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}(K_{0};q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>raw</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>raw</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}:=\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}(K_{0};q)</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A1.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ A one-shot practical calibration (heuristic; no formal guarantee). ‣ A.7 Connection to ICL (in-context learning) and experimental suggestions ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>).
We then set</p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\;:=\;\operatorname{median}_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}}\frac{\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}}{\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>median</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>cal</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>knee</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>raw</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\;:=\;\operatorname{median}_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}}\frac{\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}}{\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and freeze <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> for all reported test results.
Equivalently, the ratio between the uncalibrated and calibrated predictions is <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}/K^{\mathrm{cal}}=1/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>raw</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>cal</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}/K^{\mathrm{cal}}=1/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theoretical meaning</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> as a proxy for ICL stability can be justified in a standard ridge/linearized view: the inverse Gram matrix amplifies perturbations, and a spectral floor prevents this amplification.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Spectral floor implies ridge stability)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> have rows <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x_{i})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x_{i})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\frac{1}{K}H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\frac{1}{K}H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the ridge predictor</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x)\;:=\;\phi(x)^{\top}(H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}H_{K}^{\top}y,\qquad\lambda&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x)\;:=\;\phi(x)^{\top}(H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}H_{K}^{\top}y,\qquad\lambda&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|(H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}\big\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{K\delta+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|(H_{K}^{\top}H_{K}+\lambda I)^{-1}\big\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{K\delta+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, for any query <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and any perturbation <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta y\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta y\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y+\Delta y)-\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y)\big|\;\leq\;\frac{\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\,\|H_{K}^{\top}\Delta y\|_{2}}{K\delta+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y+\Delta y)-\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y)\big|\;\leq\;\frac{\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\,\|H_{K}^{\top}\Delta y\|_{2}}{K\delta+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if only one demonstration label <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> changes by at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y^{\prime})-\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y)\big|\;\leq\;\frac{\Delta\,\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\,\|\phi(x_{j})\|_{2}}{K\delta+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y^{\prime})-\widehat{f}_{S_{K}}(x;y)\big|\;\leq\;\frac{\Delta\,\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\,\|\phi(x_{j})\|_{2}}{K\delta+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3 (Spectral floor implies ridge stability). ‣ Theoretical meaning ‣ A.7 Connection to ICL (in-context learning) and experimental suggestions ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> makes the proxy explicit: when <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded away from zero, the fitted predictor is less sensitive to demo-level perturbations (and its variance under standard noise models is correspondingly reduced).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical application of the spectral coverage proxy.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The spectral coverage proxy provides a practitioner-ready diagnostic for estimating the minimal prompt length required for stable ICL. In practice, one can:</p>
<ol id="A1.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Extract embeddings for a set of candidate demonstrations using a fixed encoder (e.g., <span id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">all-mpnet-base-v2</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compute the empirical second-moment matrix <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\phi(x_{i})\phi(x_{i})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\phi(x_{i})\phi(x_{i})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for different values of <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{8,16,32,64\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{8,16,32,64\}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Calculate the regularized minimum eigenvalue <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=10^{-6}\cdot\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=10^{-6}\cdot\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})/d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Identify the smallest <math id="A1.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="A1.I5.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.I5.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is a task-specific threshold (e.g., <math id="A1.I5.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.1\cdot\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.1\cdot\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}\|</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As a concrete example, on the SST-2 sentiment classification task with <span id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">all-mpnet-base-v2</span> embeddings, we observed that <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> exceeded 0.1 for <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 16</annotation></semantics></math>, which closely matched the empirical knee-point of 15-18 demonstrations. This proxy can be computed offline without querying the target LLM, making it a cost-effective tool for prompt design. The validation-only calibration procedure (Section <a href="#A1.SS7" title="A.7 Connection to ICL (in-context learning) and experimental suggestions ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>) further refines this estimate by learning task-specific scaling factors on a small held-out set.
Specifically, we examine (i) tail behavior and concentration of encoder features, (ii) representation drift induced by prompt composition via controlled demo perturbations, and (iii) how spectral statistics (e.g., <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho})</annotation></semantics></math>) correlate with empirical stability and knee points.
These diagnostics support using the nominal assumption as a useful approximation, while the relaxed extensions in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Extensions Beyond the Nominal Assumption ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> capture systematic deviations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Synthetic stress tests.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further validate our theoretical claims, we perform controlled synthetic stress tests
(Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Synthetic Stress Tests ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>) by introducing bounded drift, heavy-tailed features,
and temporal dependence.
Across all cases, we find that empirical knee-points increase smoothly with the violation strength,
in line with our robustness extensions, confirming that the lower bound remains
a conservative but reliable predictor of ICL stability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark on interpretation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While we use <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> as a stability proxy, we recognize that it can be conservative and may not fully capture all sources of instability (e.g. attention saturation). Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a> provides robustness analyses, alternative spectral surrogates, and empirical diagnostics that validate and calibrate this proxy. In our experiments under fixed decoding strategies and temperature settings, we empirically observe that the saturation (knee-point) of accuracy frequently coincides with a pronounced reduction in output variability induced by different sampled demonstrations. This empirical co-occurrence suggests that accuracy knee-points can serve as a practical proxy for distributional stability in such settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Use of large language models.</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used large language models (LLMs) in two limited ways.
First, for <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">aid or polish writing</em>, an LLM service (provider redacted for anonymous review) helped with grammar, style, and tightening of sentences.
All technical content, problem formulations, theorems, proofs, algorithmic designs, model implementations, experiments, and final claims were authored and verified by the authors.
Second, for <em id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">retrieval and discovery</em>, we used LLM-assisted search to expand keyword queries and to draft short summaries of candidate papers from public abstracts.
Inclusion decisions and all citations were made only after the authors read the original sources; no autogenerated references were accepted.
No private or proprietary data were provided to the LLM, and prompts contained only our own drafts or publicly available text.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Reproducibility Specification</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides an executable specification of our experimental pipeline.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Datasets and splits</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate (i) text classification tasks: SST-2, AGNews, Yahoo! Answers (Topics), and TREC-6;
(ii) multi-step reasoning: GSM8K (and SVAMP in extended ablations); and
(iii) retrieval-augmented generation (RAG): HotpotQA (and NaturalQuestions in extended ablations).
Unless otherwise stated, for each task we use the standard public train/test split.
Demonstrations are sampled from the training split; evaluation queries are drawn from the test split.
For calibration (when used), we draw a small validation subset from the training split only
(never from the test split) to avoid test leakage.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Prompt template and label mapping</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All ICL prompts follow the same canonical format, with <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations followed by a query:</p>
<blockquote id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Task: {task_name}
<br class="ltx_break">You will be given an input and you must output the label. Output only the label token.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Input: {x_1}
<br class="ltx_break">Label: {y_1}
<br class="ltx_break">…
<br class="ltx_break">Input: {x_K}
<br class="ltx_break">Label: {y_K}
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Input: {x_q}
<br class="ltx_break">Label:<span id="A3.SS2.p1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Single-token labels.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To reduce output ambiguity, we use single-token labels whenever possible.
For binary tasks (e.g., SST-2), we map labels to <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> yes</span> / <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> no</span>.
For multi-class tasks, we map each class to a distinct single token (e.g., a digit token <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> 0</span>, <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> 1</span>, …),
and we provide an explicit class-to-token mapping in the prompt header.
When a dataset’s native label string is multi-token, we report results under both the native label and the
single-token remapping in the corresponding ablation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Demonstration selection and retrieval</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless an ablation specifies otherwise, we use cosine-similarity nearest-neighbor retrieval (Cosine-NN)
to form demonstrations for each query:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Embed each candidate training input <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and query <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> into a vector space (Section <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Encoders and representations ‣ Appendix C Experimental Reproducibility Specification ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rank training candidates by cosine similarity to <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and select the top-<math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> as demonstrations.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the retrieval ablation, we additionally compare: (i) random sampling; and (ii) class-balanced sampling (with equal per-class quota when feasible). Throughout, “retrieval” in this subsection refers to selecting demonstrations; evidence retrieval for RAG is specified separately in Appendix <a href="#A11" title="Appendix K Multi-step Reasoning and RAG Tasks ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Encoders and representations</h3>

<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Encoders.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use sentence-level encoders listed in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Default practical choices. ‣ 3.5 Calibration and practical recommendations ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (e.g., <span id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">all-mpnet-base-v2</span>,
<span id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">all-MiniLM-L6-v2</span>, <span id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">paraphrase-MiniLM-L12-v2</span>).
For each input text <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute a fixed embedding <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> using the encoder’s default pooling
(e.g., mean pooling over token embeddings followed by normalization if provided by the encoder).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Second-moment construction.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations selected for a query, we form the empirical second-moment matrix
<math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}e(x_{i})e(x_{i})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}e(x_{i})e(x_{i})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> from their encoder embeddings
(using the same normalization/preprocessing across all experiments).
When a ridge-shifted proxy is used, we report results with
<math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}:=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K,\rho}:=\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\rho I</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is computed once from the pilot matrix as
<math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\min\{\epsilon_{\rho}\cdot\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})/d,\ \delta/2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\min\{\epsilon_{\rho}\cdot\mathrm{tr}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}})/d,\ \delta/2\}</annotation></semantics></math>
and is then held fixed for all <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> within that run.
The coefficient <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed across runs; calibration (when enabled) tunes only <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> unless explicitly stated.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generator internal representations.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Most commercial LLM APIs do not expose internal hidden states.
Accordingly, our diagnostics focus on <em id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">observable</em> quantities (accuracy curves, knee estimates, and spectral proxies computed from external encoders).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Commercial API generators and decoding hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Between <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12.18.2025</span> and <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.15.2026</span>, we evaluate six large-scale commercial API models latest version:
OpenAI <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">gpt-5.2-chat-latest</span>;
Anthropic <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">claude-sonnet-4-5</span>;
Gemini <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">gemini-3-flash-preview</span>;
DeepSeek <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">deepseek-reasoner</span>;
Kimi <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">kimi-k2-thinking</span>;
Qwen <span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">qwen-max-latest</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Deterministic decoding.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate instability due to demonstrations rather than sampling, we use deterministic decoding whenever supported:
temperature <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0</annotation></semantics></math>, top-<math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> (and equivalent provider parameters), and greedy/argmax decoding.
We set max output to <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> label token under the single-token label mapping; in the multi-token ablation we set max output to the minimal required tokens and stop on newline/EOS.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Request logging.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each request we log: provider, model ID/alias, API endpoint/base_url, request timestamp (UTC), decoding parameters, and the raw completion.
Because provider-side models can evolve behind stable aliases, we report exact run windows and store the returned model identifier when available.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Random seeds and determinism</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All reported results average over <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> random seeds.
We use seeds <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math> and set them for Python <span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">random</span>, NumPy, and PyTorch.
For GPU runs we enable deterministic kernels when available and log the exact library versions in the run metadata.
The only stochasticity remaining under our default protocol comes from (i) data subsampling (when used) and
(ii) bootstrapping for confidence intervals.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reporting variance across seeds.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each configuration, we compute the ratio <math id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}:=K^{*}_{s}/\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee},s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>knee</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}:=K^{*}_{s}/\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee},s}</annotation></semantics></math> separately for each seed
<math id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\{0,1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\{0,1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee},s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>knee</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee},s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the seed-specific knee estimated on the test split),
and report the mean <math id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{5}\sum_{s}r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{5}\sum_{s}r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> in the main tables.
We additionally report the standard deviation <math id="A3.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\frac{1}{4}\sum_{s}(r_{s}-\bar{r})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\frac{1}{4}\sum_{s}(r_{s}-\bar{r})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the released artifact
(along with per-seed knees and accuracies), since it is often more informative than reporting variance only on accuracies.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.7 </span>K-grid, knee-point estimator, and confidence intervals</h3>

<section id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> grid.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate accuracy on a discrete grid <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> of prompt lengths:
<math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}=\{0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}=\{0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128\}</annotation></semantics></math>, truncated as needed to respect each model’s context window.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Knee-point estimator.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the curve <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(K,\mathrm{ACC}(K))\}_{K\in\mathcal{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ACC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(K,\mathrm{ACC}(K))\}_{K\in\mathcal{K}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we fit a two-segment piecewise linear model.
For each candidate split index <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (with at least two points on each side), we fit two least-squares lines on
<math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{K\leq t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{K\leq t\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{K&gt;t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{K&gt;t\}</annotation></semantics></math> and compute the sum of squared errors (SSE).
We define <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>knee</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> at the split minimizing SSE
(ties broken by choosing the smaller <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> for conservatism).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bootstrap confidence intervals.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute a <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> percentile bootstrap interval for <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>knee</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=200</annotation></semantics></math> resamples.
Each resample draws evaluation queries with replacement from the test set, recomputes <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ACC}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ACC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ACC}(K)</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> (with demonstrations formed under the same fixed protocol), and recomputes
<math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>knee</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We report the 2.5/97.5 percentiles over the <math id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> bootstrapped knees.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sanity checks.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify that the two-segment fit is not spuriously triggered by smooth saturation or noise,
we inspect representative fitted curves and confirm that the selected breakpoint aligns with a visible transition region;
we include example curves and fitted segments in the supplementary material.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.8 </span>Calibration protocol (no test leakage)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When calibration is enabled (choosing <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and fitting the global scale factor <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>),
we tune hyperparameters on a small calibration subset drawn from training data only and keep the test split untouched.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task-level split.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each encoder–generator pair, we select a small set of tasks <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>cal</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math> for calibration and a disjoint set
<math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>eval</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> for final reporting. The selection is fixed before running any test evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Within-task data split.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each task, we use the training split to form demonstrations and (when needed) to build the calibration curves.
All reported accuracies, knee-points, and final ratios are computed on the task’s test split.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fitting <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> from measured knee-points.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>cal</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we estimate <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>knee</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> using the piecewise-linear method described above,
and compute <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>raw</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A1.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ A one-shot practical calibration (heuristic; no formal guarantee). ‣ A.7 Connection to ICL (in-context learning) and experimental suggestions ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) using the pilot matrix <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We choose <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in[0.05,0.2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in[0.05,0.2]</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing the median absolute log-error on <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>cal</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\star}\in\arg\min_{q\in[0.05,0.2]}\operatorname{median}_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}}\left|\log\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}(q)-\log\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>median</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>cal</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>raw</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>knee</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\star}\in\arg\min_{q\in[0.05,0.2]}\operatorname{median}_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{cal}}}\left|\log\widehat{K}^{\mathrm{raw}}_{t}(q)-\log\widehat{K}_{\mathrm{knee}}^{(t)}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then we set <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> by the median ratio fit (<a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ How 𝛼 is determined from measured performance. ‣ A.7 Connection to ICL (in-context learning) and experimental suggestions ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) with <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=q^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=q^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, we freeze <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q^{\star},\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q^{\star},\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> and evaluate on <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>eval</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> without further tuning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Robustness Extensions</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main text, our theoretical guarantees are derived under the nominal assumption (A1),
namely that the representation <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed and sub-Gaussian with second-moment <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here we discuss how the results extend when assumptions (A2)–(A4) are considered.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Robustness to Representation Drift (A2)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider an independent but non-identically distributed (i.n.i.d.) sequence across the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in-context demonstrations.
For each context index <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be drawn independently and define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}(x)=\phi(x)+\Delta_{t}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}(x)=\phi(x)+\Delta_{t}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the drift satisfies the uniform bound <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{t}(x)\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{t}(x)\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</p>
<table id="A4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}:=\phi_{t}(x_{t})\phi_{t}(x_{t})^{\top},\qquad\Sigma_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[X_{t}],\qquad\bar{\Sigma}:=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{t=1}^{K}\Sigma_{t},\qquad\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{t=1}^{K}X_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}:=\phi_{t}(x_{t})\phi_{t}(x_{t})^{\top},\qquad\Sigma_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[X_{t}],\qquad\bar{\Sigma}:=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{t=1}^{K}\Sigma_{t},\qquad\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{t=1}^{K}X_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The goal is to control <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> via concentration of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and then relate <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> back to the nominal <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma:=\mathbb{E}[\phi(x)\phi(x)^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma:=\mathbb{E}[\phi(x)\phi(x)^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Second-moment shift under bounded drift)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{t}(x)\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{t}(x)\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, for every <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma_{t}-\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;2\varepsilon\,\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2},\qquad\text{and hence}\qquad\|\bar{\Sigma}-\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;2\varepsilon\,\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and hence</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma_{t}-\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;2\varepsilon\,\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2},\qquad\text{and hence}\qquad\|\bar{\Sigma}-\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;2\varepsilon\,\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}=\mathbb{E}[(\phi+\Delta_{t})(\phi+\Delta_{t})^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}=\mathbb{E}[(\phi+\Delta_{t})(\phi+\Delta_{t})^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}-\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[\phi\Delta_{t}^{\top}]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\phi^{\top}]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}-\Sigma=\mathbb{E}[\phi\Delta_{t}^{\top}]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\phi^{\top}]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}\preceq\|\Delta_{t}\|_{2}^{2}I\preceq\varepsilon^{2}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}\preceq\|\Delta_{t}\|_{2}^{2}I\preceq\varepsilon^{2}I</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\varepsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\varepsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the cross term, use the operator Cauchy–Schwarz inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}[\phi\Delta_{t}^{\top}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;\big\|\mathbb{E}[\phi\phi^{\top}]\big\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}\,\big\|\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}]\big\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}\;\leq\;\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}\cdot\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}[\phi\Delta_{t}^{\top}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;\big\|\mathbb{E}[\phi\phi^{\top}]\big\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}\,\big\|\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t}^{\top}]\big\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}\;\leq\;\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}\cdot\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The same bound holds for <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\phi^{\top}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}\phi^{\top}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variance-proxy derivation (i.n.i.d.).</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For matrix Bernstein in the i.n.i.d. setting, we center each summand by its own mean:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}:=X_{t}-\Sigma_{t},\qquad\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}]=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}:=X_{t}-\Sigma_{t},\qquad\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the variance parameter is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v:=\left\|\sum_{t=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;\sum_{t=1}^{K}\left\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;=\;K\cdot\max_{t}\left\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.391em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v:=\left\|\sum_{t=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;\leq\;\sum_{t=1}^{K}\left\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}\;=\;K\cdot\max_{t}\left\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We now bound <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly under drift.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance proxy under bounded drift)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}=X_{t}-\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}=X_{t}-\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}=\phi_{t}\phi_{t}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}=\phi_{t}\phi_{t}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta_{t}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta_{t}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for every <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}+2\,\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}+2\,\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}+2\,\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}+2\,\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 16C_{1}\sigma^{4}\;+\;48\,\varepsilon^{2}\,\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)\;+\;16\varepsilon^{4}\;+\;2\big(\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}+2\varepsilon\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2}\big)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 48</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 16C_{1}\sigma^{4}\;+\;48\,\varepsilon^{2}\,\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)\;+\;16\varepsilon^{4}\;+\;2\big(\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}+2\varepsilon\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2}\big)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fourth-moment constant from (A1) (i.e., <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|_{2}^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|_{2}^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the noncommutative square inequality <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A-B)^{2}\preceq 2A^{2}+2B^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A-B)^{2}\preceq 2A^{2}+2B^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for symmetric <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ A noncommutative square inequality. ‣ A.2.1 Fourth-moment bound ‣ A.2 Controlling 𝑅,𝑣̃ under the sub-Gaussian assumption (truncation and fourth-moment bounds) ‣ Appendix A Complete Theory Chain ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) in the main text),
we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}^{2}=(X_{t}-\Sigma_{t})^{2}\preceq 2X_{t}^{2}+2\Sigma_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}^{2}=(X_{t}-\Sigma_{t})^{2}\preceq 2X_{t}^{2}+2\Sigma_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation and operator norm, and using <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}[M]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\mathbb{E}\|M\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}[M]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\mathbb{E}\|M\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}^{2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}+2\|\Sigma_{t}^{2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}=2\,\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}+2\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}^{2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}+2\|\Sigma_{t}^{2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}=2\,\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}+2\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X_{t}^{2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}=\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X_{t}^{2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}=\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Next, <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}=\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}=\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|X_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To bound <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, use <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}\leq\|\phi\|_{2}+\|\Delta_{t}\|_{2}\leq\|\phi\|_{2}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}\leq\|\phi\|_{2}+\|\Delta_{t}\|_{2}\leq\|\phi\|_{2}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and the inequality
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a+b)^{4}\leq 8a^{4}+24a^{2}b^{2}+8b^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a+b)^{4}\leq 8a^{4}+24a^{2}b^{2}+8b^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}\leq 8\|\phi\|_{2}^{4}+24\varepsilon^{2}\|\phi\|_{2}^{2}+8\varepsilon^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}\leq 8\|\phi\|_{2}^{4}+24\varepsilon^{2}\|\phi\|_{2}^{2}+8\varepsilon^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation and using <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|_{2}^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|_{2}^{4}\leq C_{1}\sigma^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|_{2}^{2}=\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\phi\|_{2}^{2}=\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}\leq 8C_{1}\sigma^{4}+24\varepsilon^{2}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)+8\varepsilon^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\phi_{t}\|_{2}^{4}\leq 8C_{1}\sigma^{4}+24\varepsilon^{2}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma)+8\varepsilon^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1 (Second-moment shift under bounded drift). ‣ D.1 Robustness to Representation Drift (A2) ‣ Appendix D Robustness Extensions ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}+2\varepsilon\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}+2\varepsilon\|\Sigma\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}+\varepsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining the bounds proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Robustness under bounded drift (with explicit variance proxy))<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under (A2), apply matrix Bernstein to the independent centered matrices <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}=X_{t}-\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}=X_{t}-\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> be the Bernstein variance parameter and let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be any almost-sure bound on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Y_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Y_{t}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> after truncation (as in the main proof technique).
Then for any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\left\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\bar{\Sigma}\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}\geq\eta\right)\;\leq\;d\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{K\eta^{2}/2}{v+B\eta/3}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\left\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\bar{\Sigma}\right\|_{\mathrm{op}}\geq\eta\right)\;\leq\;d\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{K\eta^{2}/2}{v+B\eta/3}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Variance proxy under bounded drift). ‣ Variance-proxy derivation (i.n.i.d.). ‣ D.1 Robustness to Representation Drift (A2) ‣ Appendix D Robustness Extensions ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> provides an explicit <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent upper bound on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> (via <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\leq K\max_{t}\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\leq K\max_{t}\|\mathbb{E}[Y_{t}^{2}]\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>),
and Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1 (Second-moment shift under bounded drift). ‣ D.1 Robustness to Representation Drift (A2) ‣ Appendix D Robustness Extensions ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> relates <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> back to <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, whenever <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&lt;\lambda_{\min}(\bar{\Sigma})-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&lt;\lambda_{\min}(\bar{\Sigma})-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the event
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\bar{\Sigma}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}-\bar{\Sigma}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math> implies</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\lambda_{\min}(\bar{\Sigma})-\eta\geq\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\lambda_{\min}(\bar{\Sigma})-\eta\geq\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Relaxing Tail Assumptions (A3)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is only sub-exponential or has bounded fourth moments,
then <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi(x)\|^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi(x)\|^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> has heavier tails.
In this case, truncation plus Bernstein inequality yields an adjusted bound of the form</p>
<table id="A4.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\;\gtrsim\;\frac{(\|\Sigma\|^{2}+\sigma^{4}+\kappa^{2})}{(\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-\delta)^{2}}\,\mathrm{polylog}(d/\xi)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≳</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>polylog</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\;\gtrsim\;\frac{(\|\Sigma\|^{2}+\sigma^{4}+\kappa^{2})}{(\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-\delta)^{2}}\,\mathrm{polylog}(d/\xi),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is a moment constant.
The dependence on <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> reflects the heavier tails, but the overall scaling remains quadratic in the spectral gap.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Weak Dependence among Features (A4)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi_{t}(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi_{t}(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> are not independent across <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
we apply matrix concentration for martingale-difference or <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-mixing sequences .
In this case, the effective sample size is reduced:
if the mixing coefficient is <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, then the bound takes the same form as in Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem D.3 (Robustness under bounded drift (with explicit variance proxy)). ‣ Variance-proxy derivation (i.n.i.d.). ‣ D.1 Robustness to Representation Drift (A2) ‣ Appendix D Robustness Extensions ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>,
with <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/(1+\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/(1+\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus moderate dependence inflates the sample complexity by at most a constant factor.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Summary</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these results demonstrate that our main lower bound is <em id="A4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">robust</em>:
when the representation drifts mildly, exhibits heavier tails, or has weak temporal dependence,
the sufficient sample-size requirement increases smoothly and predictably,
rather than collapsing.
In practice, this means that the nominal bound from (A1) can still be used as a conservative guideline,
while deviations are accommodated by additive or multiplicative correction factors.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Extensions to Dependent Features</h2>

<figure id="A5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A5.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Notation and constants used across sections.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A5.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Symbol</td>
<td id="A5.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Meaning / Where defined</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A5.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma,\ \|\Sigma\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma,\ \|\Sigma\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
