<span id="A6.T4.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="A6.T4.5.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\;\geq\;K_{\mathrm{nominal}}+g(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>nominal</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\;\geq\;K_{\mathrm{nominal}}+g(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A6.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> grows polynomially in <math id="A6.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and spectral ratios</span>
</span></td></tr>
