<span id="A6.T4.5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">(A4) Dependence</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A6.T4.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:148.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T4.5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Features form a martingale-difference sequence or <math id="A6.T4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-mixing process with coefficient <math id="A6.T4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T4.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A6.T4.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:184.9pt;">
<span id="A6.T4.5.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Effective sample size
<math id="A6.T4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathrm{eff}}\approx\tfrac{K}{1+c_{\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathrm{eff}}\approx\tfrac{K}{1+c_{\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so bound inflates by factor <math id="A6.T4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+c_{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+c_{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
