<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observation.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Heavier tails inflate the required prompt length by a multiplicative constant,
but truncation or normalization substantially reduces the inflation.
This behavior aligns with the extended bound in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Extensions Beyond the Nominal Assumption ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Temporal Dependence</h3>

<figure id="A7.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A7.T8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="A7.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Dependence stress test results (<math id="A7.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=100</annotation></semantics></math>).
<math id="A7.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathrm{nominal}}=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>nominal</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathrm{nominal}}=32</annotation></semantics></math>.
Effective sample size <math id="A7.T8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> decreases with <math id="A7.T8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
