<td id="A7.T8.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">32</td>
<td id="A7.T8.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">70 <math id="A7.T8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> 8</td>
<td id="A7.T8.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">38</td>
<td id="A7.T8.5.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">16</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A7.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observation.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Empirical knee-points scale approximately as <math id="A7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+c_{\rho})\cdot K_{\mathrm{nominal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>nominal</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+c_{\rho})\cdot K_{\mathrm{nominal}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
consistent with our dependence extension in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Extensions to Dependent Features ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.5 </span>Summary</h3>

<div id="A7.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across all three stress tests,
the empirical knee-point increases smoothly with the violation strength,
either additively (drift), multiplicatively (tails), or by a dependence factor (temporal correlation).
These controlled experiments confirm that our non-asymptotic lower bound is
robust: violations of (A1) shift the threshold conservatively,
but do not invalidate the predictive power of <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> as a proxy for ICL stability.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Interpretability of the Proxy</h2>

<div id="A8.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition H.1</span></span><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Predictive variance control via <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the design with rows <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x_{k})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x_{k})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}=\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}=\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>.
For ridge predictor
<math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}(x)=\phi(x)^{\top}\!\left(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\frac{\lambda}{K}I\right)^{\!-1}\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}(x)=\phi(x)^{\top}\!\left(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\frac{\lambda}{K}I\right)^{\!-1}\frac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y</annotation></semantics></math>,
if <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\widehat{f}(x_{\star})\mid\Phi\right)\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\delta+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\widehat{f}(x_{\star})\mid\Phi\right)\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\delta+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">See <a href="#A8.SS1" title="H.1 Proof sketch of Proposition ‣ Appendix H Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.1</span></a> for details; it follows by the matrix inequality
<math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}(K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}(K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=K\widehat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>
and the Rayleigh quotient bound <math id="A8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}^{\top}A^{-1}\mathbf{v}\leq\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}^{\top}A^{-1}\mathbf{v}\leq\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Theoretical link.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#A8.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition H.1 (Predictive variance control via 𝜆_min). ‣ Appendix H Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.1</span></a> (Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>) shows that
a lower bound on <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>
suffices to control predictive variance of in-context regression,
providing a mechanistic rationale for why it correlates with stability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Limitations.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">However, <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> can be overly conservative in practice:
(i) tiny eigenvalues with negligible test alignment,
(ii) heavy tails beyond sub-Gaussian assumptions,
(iii) contextual dependence that alters effective conditioning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alternative surrogates.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We therefore also consider quantile eigenvalues <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the condition number <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, effective rank <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and average leverage scores.
These quantities often correlate more closely with empirical knee-points.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Calibration.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A light calibration step (estimating a global scale <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>
and quantile level <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> on a small validation set)
substantially improves predictive accuracy of the proxy
(see Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Default practical choices. ‣ 3.5 Calibration and practical recommendations ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Proof sketch of Proposition</h3>

<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the design matrix with rows <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x_{k})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x_{k})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and denote <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Sigma}_{K}:=\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume the response obeys <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}=f^{\star}(x_{k})+\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with homoscedastic noise
<math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext>i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi(x)\|_{2}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.
Consider the ridge predictor</p>
<table id="A8.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x)~=~\phi(x)^{\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\cdot\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y\Bigr),\quad\lambda\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x)~=~\phi(x)^{\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\cdot\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}y\Bigr),\quad\lambda\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For a fixed test point <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\star}:=\phi(x^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\star}:=\phi(x^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Linear form and conditional variance.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Conditioned on the design <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> is linear in <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x^{\star})=a^{\top}y,\qquad a^{\top}=\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x^{\star})=a^{\top}y,\qquad a^{\top}=\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\tfrac{1}{K}\Phi^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(y\mid\Phi)=\sigma^{2}I_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(y\mid\Phi)=\sigma^{2}I_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A8.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\|a\|_{2}^{2}~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\phi^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\|a\|_{2}^{2}~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\Bigl(\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\tfrac{\lambda}{K}I\Bigr)^{-1}\phi^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, with <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A8.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\,(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\,A^{-1}\phi^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~=~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\,(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\,A^{-1}\phi^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: matrix inequality.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\preceq A=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\preceq A=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{-1/2}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1/2}\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1/2}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1/2}\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</p>
<table id="A8.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{-1}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1}(K\hat{\Sigma}_{K})A^{-1}\preceq A^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Plugging into (<a href="#A8.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Linear form and conditional variance. ‣ H.1 Proof sketch of Proposition ‣ Appendix H Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A8.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\sigma^{2}\,\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Rayleigh quotient bound.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> and vector <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}M^{-1}v\leq\|v\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}M^{-1}v\leq\|v\|_{2}^{2}/\lambda_{\min}(M)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=K\hat{\Sigma}_{K}+\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\phi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\phi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A8.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}~\leq~\frac{\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}~\leq~\frac{B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>⋆</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\star\top}A^{-1}\phi^{\star}~\leq~\frac{\|\phi^{\star}\|_{2}^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}~\leq~\frac{B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Combining with (<a href="#A8.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Step 1: matrix inequality. ‣ H.1 Proof sketch of Proposition ‣ Appendix H Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A8.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\hat{f}(x^{\star})\mid\Phi\right)~\leq~\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\,\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})+\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusion.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, whenever <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A8.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\hat{f}(x^{\star}))\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\delta+\lambda}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\hat{f}(x^{\star}))\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma^{2}B^{2}}{K\delta+\lambda},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which establishes Proposition <a href="#A8.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition H.1 (Predictive variance control via 𝜆_min). ‣ Appendix H Interpretability of the Proxy ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.1</span></a>.
 <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) If <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the result still holds provided <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Sigma}_{K}\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
(ii) For heteroscedastic noise, the bound uses the maximal variance.
(iii) Under model misspecification, bias terms can be separated, and the variance part remains controlled by <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(\hat{\Sigma}_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Ablation Studies</h2>

<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overview.</h5>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To bridge the gap between theory and practice, we performed ten ablations that correspond to the key factors appearing in our formula and experimental pipeline. We first present a summary table that aggregates all results, followed by ten dedicated <span id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">“subsection</span>s, each restating its own result with brief analysis and takeaway. All numbers are averages over multiple runs unless otherwise noted, and error ratios are defined as theoretical <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> divided by the empirical knee (lower is better).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.1 </span><math id="A9.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-ratio Sensitivity</h3>

<div id="A9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Increasing <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math> reduces the theoretical upper bound from <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}\!\approx\!95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mn>95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}\!\approx\!95</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}\!\approx\!25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}\!\approx\!25</annotation></semantics></math>, with error ratio decreasing from <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.3\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.4\times</annotation></semantics></math>. The mechanism is through the effective spectral gap <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\lambda_{\min}(\Sigma)-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Numerically, <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> acts like a conservativeness amplifier. Theoretically, it encodes a robustness margin on <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>. Mathematically, it discounts the least eigenvalue to stabilize finite-sample estimation. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Correct scaling w.r.t. <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (using <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\rho\,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\rho\,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and pick an anchor <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A9.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}(\rho)=K^{*}(\rho_{0})\left(\frac{1-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho\,}\right)^{\!2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}(\rho)=K^{*}(\rho_{0})\left(\frac{1-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho\,}\right)^{\!2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For example, from <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.9</annotation></semantics></math> the factor is <math id="A9.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="81\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>81</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">81\times</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.2 </span>Effective Rank Definition</h3>

<div id="A9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Rank estimation method strongly affects tightness: thresholding gives <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math>, energy-based <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 2.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>2.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2.4\times</annotation></semantics></math>, and trace-based <math id="A9.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> The definition operationalizes model complexity. Threshold is safest but loosest; energy balances dominant and tail directions; trace emphasizes overall spread. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Rank definition</td>
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Threshold</td>
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Energy</td>
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 2.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>2.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2.4\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Trace</td>
<td id="A9.SS2.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.3 </span>Sub-Gaussian Parameter <math id="A9.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A9.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Increasing <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.0</annotation></semantics></math> scales <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by several times, sometimes approaching an order-of-magnitude increase. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Numerically, <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a dominant driver of between-task variability. Theoretically, it reflects tail decay and concentration strength. Mathematically, it is the constant in sub-Gaussian concentration appearing in upper bounds. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS3.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A9.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS3.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Qualitative effect on <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS3.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS3.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">small</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS3.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS3.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">several<math id="A9.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> larger</td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.4 </span>Second-moment Norm <math id="A9.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Sigma\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Sigma\|</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A9.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Using the spectral norm typically yields <math id="A9.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios, Frobenius yields <math id="A9.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math>, while mean-variance approximations can under-estimate and approach <math id="A9.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Spectral norm focuses on the hardest direction; Frobenius spreads mass across all directions; rough mean-variance may miss heavy directions and be overly optimistic. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Norm choice</td>
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Spectral</td>
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Frobenius</td>
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Mean-variance</td>
<td id="A9.SS4.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1\times</annotation></semantics></math> (may under-estimate)</td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.5 </span>Label Tokenization</h3>

<div id="A9.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Single-token labels (e.g., <span id="A9.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">yes/no</span>, <span id="A9.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">POS/NEG</span>) yield smaller knees and <math id="A9.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios, whereas multi-token labels (e.g., <span id="A9.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">positive/negative</span>) often exceed <math id="A9.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Single-token labels shrink the effective output search space. Multi-token labels dilute probability mass and inflate the required <math id="A9.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Tokenization</td>
<td id="A9.SS5.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS5.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Single-token</td>
<td id="A9.SS5.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS5.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS5.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Multi-token</td>
<td id="A9.SS5.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\geq 3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 3\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.6 </span>Prompt Truncation Policy</h3>

<div id="A9.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> <em id="A9.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Latest-first</em> delivers smaller knees and <math id="A9.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios; <em id="A9.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">earliest-first</em> shifts the knee right and often exceeds <math id="A9.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math>; random truncation increases variance across runs. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Latest-first respects the model inductive bias toward local context; earliest-first tends to retain stale or less relevant examples; random adds sampling noise. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Policy</td>
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS6.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Latest-first</td>
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS6.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Earliest-first</td>
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="&gt;3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;3\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS6.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Random</td>
<td id="A9.SS6.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">larger variance</td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.7 </span>Theory Constant Scaling</h3>

<div id="A9.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> A global scale <math id="A9.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}_{\text{adj}}=C\cdot K^{*}_{\text{theory}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mtext>adj</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mtext>theory</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}_{\text{adj}}=C\cdot K^{*}_{\text{theory}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A9.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\approx 10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≈</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\approx 10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> systematically tightens predictions to <math id="A9.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Numerically, <math id="A9.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a cross-task calibrator. Theoretically, it compensates for conservative constants in concentration bounds. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS7.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A9.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS7.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Typical error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS7.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS7.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">∼</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}\!\sim\!10^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS7.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS7.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS7.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS7.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math> (uncalibrated)</td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.8 </span>Synthetic Data Experiments</h3>

<div id="A9.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Under controlled Gaussian features with known <math id="A9.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, the theory-to-practice gap shrinks to <math id="A9.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> This indicates that the larger gaps on real data primarily arise from violations of sub-Gaussian tails, linear separability, or spectral stability. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS8.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Setting</td>
<td id="A9.SS8.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS8.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS8.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Controlled Gaussian</td>
<td id="A9.SS8.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS8.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS8.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Real tasks</td>
<td id="A9.SS8.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.9 </span>Retrieval Strategy</h3>

<div id="A9.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> Cosine-similarity nearest neighbor retrieval yields the smallest knees and <math id="A9.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> error ratios; random sampling degrades stability and often exceeds <math id="A9.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.5\times</annotation></semantics></math>; class-balanced sampling lies between. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Retrieval reshapes the empirical second-moment around the test point, preserving a larger effective <math id="A9.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and tightening <math id="A9.SS9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Retrieval</td>
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS9.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Cosine-NN</td>
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS9.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS9.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Balanced</td>
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">intermediate</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS9.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Random</td>
<td id="A9.SS9.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS9.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\geq 2.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 2.5\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.10 </span>Model Scale</h3>

<div id="A9.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result.</span> On SST-2, the empirical knee decreases from <math id="A9.SS10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 12</annotation></semantics></math> for a 124M model to <math id="A9.SS10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 7</annotation></semantics></math> for a 345M model, with the error ratio dropping from <math id="A9.SS10.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS10.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.2\times</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Larger models better exploit demonstrations and align more closely with theoretical assumptions (smaller effective noise, more stable spectra). 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A9.SS10.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mini-table.</span></p>
<table id="A9.SS10.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.SS10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Model</td>
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Knee (SST-2)</td>
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Error ratio</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS10.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">124M</td>
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 12</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A9.SS10.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.4\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.SS10.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">345M</td>
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 7</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.SS10.p1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A9.SS10.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.2\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Closing remarks.</h5>

<div id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across the ten axes, three levers consistently tighten the theory-to-practice gap: (i) increasing the effective spectral gap (via <math id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> choice, retrieval near the test point, and stable norm definitions), (ii) reducing effective noise (smaller <math id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, single-token labels, larger models), and (iii) cross-task calibration of conservative constants (<math id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-scaling). Under idealized assumptions validated by synthetic data, the gap nearly vanishes; on real tasks, careful choices along these levers reduce error ratios toward <math id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A9.SS10.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> while preserving reproducibility.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Theoretical Constants: Sources, Mappings, and Practical Calibration</h2>

<section id="A10.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.1 </span>List of Constants and Quick Reference</h3>

<div id="A10.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A10.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ J.1 List of Constants and Quick Reference ‣ Appendix J Theoretical Constants: Sources, Mappings, and Practical Calibration ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> summarizes all explicit or implicit constants, structural factors, and engineering fudge factors appearing in the paper. The following subsections provide:
(i) theoretical origins and geometric interpretations;
(ii) quantitative coupling with problem parameters (dimension <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, effective rank <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, signal-to-noise ratio, confidence level <math id="A10.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>);
(iii) a three-step experimental calibration guideline (simulation–calibration–cross-validation).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A10.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A10.T9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="A10.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Constants and recommended values</span></figcaption>
<table id="A10.T9.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A10.T9.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A10.T9.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Symbol</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Type</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Occurrence</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Recommended Range</td></tr>
<tr id="A10.T9.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A10.T9.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A10.T9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2,\,2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2,\,2/3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Structural</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Matrix Bernstein tail bound</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Fixed, non-tunable</td></tr>
<tr id="A10.T9.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A10.T9.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><math id="A10.T9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">Absolute</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">Fourth-moment bound</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><math id="A10.T9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1.5,6]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1.5,6]</annotation></semantics></math>, recommend <math id="A10.T9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A10.T9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.T9.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A10.T9.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><math id="A10.T9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">Absolute</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">Second-moment deviation bound</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><math id="A10.T9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2,4]</annotation></semantics></math>, recommend <math id="A10.T9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A10.T9.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A10.T9.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r"><math id="A10.T9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime},\,c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime},\,c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r">Engineering</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r">Sample-size formulae</td>
<td id="A10.T9.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r"><math id="A10.T9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 8</annotation></semantics></math>, typically <math id="A10.T9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A10.T9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.2 </span>Theoretical Origins and Geometric Interpretation</h3>

<section id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Matrix Bernstein constants <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the sum of independent centered random matrices <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\sum Y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\sum Y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A10.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\lambda_{\min}(S)\leq-t\right)\;\leq\;r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2v+\tfrac{2}{3}Rt}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\lambda_{\min}(S)\leq-t\right)\;\leq\;r_{\mathrm{eff}}\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2v+\tfrac{2}{3}Rt}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The coefficients <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/3</annotation></semantics></math> arise from the moment-generating-function method and are structural, non-adjustable constants.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sub-Gaussian fourth-moment constant <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a mean-zero sub-Gaussian vector <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, an absolute constant <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures</p>
<table id="A10.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{4}\;\leq\;c_{1}\;\bigl(\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{2}\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{4}\;\leq\;c_{1}\;\bigl(\mathbb{E}\|Z\|^{2}\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Examples:</p>
<ul id="A10.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A10.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gaussian: <math id="A10.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A10.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uniform on sphere: <math id="A10.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\approx 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\approx 3</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rademacher: <math id="A10.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\approx 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\approx 3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For anisotropic distributions, <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> scales with the condition number <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(\Sigma)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\Sigma)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, after standardization and with <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 50</annotation></semantics></math>, simulations suggest <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\in[1.5,6]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\in[1.5,6]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> recommended.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">second-moment operator deviation constant <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Koltchinskii &amp; Lounici proved</p>
<table id="A10.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\Sigma}-\Sigma\|\;\leq\;c_{2}\|\Sigma\|\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}}+\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\Sigma}-\Sigma\|\;\leq\;c_{2}\|\Sigma\|\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}}+\tfrac{r(\Sigma)t}{n}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Typical values:</p>
<ul id="A10.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A10.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sub-Gaussian: <math id="A10.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=2</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sub-exponential: <math id="A10.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=4</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finite fourth moment: <math id="A10.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> scales with kurtosis <math id="A10.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Empirically, <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=3</annotation></semantics></math> suffices in 95% of cases for <math id="A10.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d/n\in[0.1,0.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d/n\in[0.1,0.5]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.3 </span>Coupling with Problem Parameters</h3>

<div id="A10.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main sample-size requirement is</p>
<table id="A10.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\;\geq\;c^{\prime}\cdot r(\Sigma)\,\frac{t+\log d}{\varepsilon^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\;\geq\;c^{\prime}\cdot r(\Sigma)\,\frac{t+\log d}{\varepsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Implications:</p>
<ul id="A10.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A10.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A10.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> influences estimation error of the effective rank <math id="A10.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A10.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> scales the relative error <math id="A10.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> directly;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Structural constants <math id="A10.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2,2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2,2/3</annotation></semantics></math> remain fixed;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Engineering factors <math id="A10.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime},c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime},c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> ensure practical safety, typically increasing with confidence level <math id="A10.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.4 </span>Three-Step Calibration Procedure</h3>

<div id="A10.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A10.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A10.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A10.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulation calibration:</span> Generate synthetic Gaussian datasets across <math id="A10.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,n)</annotation></semantics></math> grids, estimate failure probabilities, and back out <math id="A10.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> with 95% quantile anchoring.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A10.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robustness to misspecification:</span> Test under sub-exponential, heavy-tailed, and real bootstrap data. If <math id="A10.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> inflates more than <math id="A10.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\times</annotation></semantics></math>, adjust by <math id="A10.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa/5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A10.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-validation locking of <math id="A10.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime},c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime},c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> On real data, run two-stage procedures with 5-fold cross-validation, plot error–sample size curves, and infer <math id="A10.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from the plateau point.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">J.5 </span>Default practical choices</h3>

<div id="A10.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across tasks, we recommend:
(i) a modest ridge <math id="A10.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> to stabilize inversion and dampen near-null directions;
(ii) choosing <math id="A10.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A10.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>) as a fraction of the pilot spectrum, e.g., proportional to
<math id="A10.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{q}(\widehat{\Sigma}_{K_{0},\rho})</annotation></semantics></math>; and
(iii) splitting the failure budget evenly across the two stages (as in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 An observable two-stage estimator ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)
unless one stage is known to dominate the uncertainty.
These choices are heuristic but align with the role of <math id="A10.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3.2 Sample complexity bound ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>):
larger margins reduce the required <math id="A10.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and ridge improves numerical stability when <math id="A10.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is ill-conditioned.</p>
</div>
<section id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choosing the target floor <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and handling infeasible targets.</h5>

<div id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proxy objective in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Intuition and example. ‣ 3.1 Problem setup and proxy objective ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is parameterized by a target spectral floor <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,
which controls how well-conditioned the demonstration second moment must be to certify the surrogate stability event.
In Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 An observable two-stage estimator ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the check <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}=\underline{\lambda}-\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}=\underline{\lambda}-\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is necessary; if the algorithm returns <span id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">infeasible target</span>,
it means that the requested <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is larger than the estimated population floor at the desired confidence level, under the current feature map and ridge level.
In practice we recommend selecting <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> by validation: sweep <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> on a small held-out set, choose the smallest value that achieves the desired stability/accuracy trade-off,
and then lock it for test-time estimation.
When available, Appendix <a href="#A12" title="Appendix L Direct Measurement of Distributional Stability (Definition 3.1) ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">L</span></a> provides a direct estimator for distributional stability in the sense of Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1 (ICL stability at (𝜏,𝜉)). ‣ 3.1 Problem setup and proxy objective ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> that can serve as the validation signal.
If infeasibility persists, reduce <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, increase the ridge via <math id="A10.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, or use the quantile-floor variant described in Section <a href="#S3.SS5" title="3.5 Calibration and practical recommendations ‣ 3 Theory ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A11" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix K </span>Multi-step Reasoning and RAG Tasks</h2>

<div id="A11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix specifies the experimental protocol for multi-step reasoning and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG).
Unless stated otherwise, knee estimation, bootstrap CIs, and calibration follow Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Experimental Reproducibility Specification ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A11.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">K.1 </span>Multi-step reasoning (GSM8K / SVAMP)</h3>

<section id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt template (final answer only).</h5>

<div id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We constrain outputs to a canonical final-answer format to reduce ambiguity while preserving multi-step computation.
Each prompt contains <math id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations followed by a query:</p>
<blockquote id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Task: Grade-school math word problems.
<br class="ltx_break">Solve the problem and output only the final numeric answer.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: {q_1}
<br class="ltx_break">A: {a_1}
<br class="ltx_break">…
<br class="ltx_break">Q: {q_K}
<br class="ltx_break">A: {a_K}
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: {q_q}
<br class="ltx_break">A:<span id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Example (one demo + one query).</h5>

<div id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Task: Grade-school math word problems.
<br class="ltx_break">Solve the problem and output only the final numeric answer.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: Lily has 12 candies. She gives 5 to her friend. How many candies does she have left?
<br class="ltx_break">A: 7
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: A store sold 18 apples in the morning and 27 in the afternoon. How many apples were sold in total?
<br class="ltx_break">A:<span id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We normalize the produced answer string (strip spaces/punctuation) and compute exact match against the gold final answer.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> grid.</h5>

<div id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Due to longer outputs, we optionally use a cost-aware grid <math id="A11.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64\}</annotation></semantics></math> (or a prefix thereof).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">K.2 </span>RAG (HotpotQA / NaturalQuestions)</h3>

<section id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Retrieval.</h5>

<div id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We retrieve top-<math id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> evidence passages per query (default <math id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=5</annotation></semantics></math>) from a fixed corpus snapshot using a deterministic retriever (e.g., BM25).
The retrieved set for each query is held fixed across all <math id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt template (evidence before demos).</h5>

<div id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We place evidence before demonstrations to reduce interleaving artifacts:</p>
<blockquote id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Task: Answer the question using the evidence. Output only the short final answer.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Evidence:
<br class="ltx_break">[1] {p_1}
<br class="ltx_break">…
<br class="ltx_break">[m] {p_m}
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: {q_1}
<br class="ltx_break">A: {a_1}
<br class="ltx_break">…
<br class="ltx_break">Q: {q_K}
<br class="ltx_break">A: {a_K}
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: {q_q}
<br class="ltx_break">A:<span id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Example (evidence + one demo + one query).</h5>

<div id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Task: Answer the question using the evidence. Output only the short final answer.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Evidence:
<br class="ltx_break">[1] Marie Curie was a physicist and chemist who conducted pioneering research on radioactivity.
<br class="ltx_break">[2] She won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1903 and the Nobel Prize in Chemistry in 1911.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: How many Nobel Prizes did Marie Curie win?
<br class="ltx_break">A: 2
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Q: In what year did Marie Curie win the Nobel Prize in Chemistry?
<br class="ltx_break">A:<span id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We score exact match and token-level F1 using the dataset’s standard evaluation protocol with standard normalization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Spectral proxy under RAG.</h5>

<div id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By default, representations <math id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are computed from the <em id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">question text only</em> to avoid retrieved evidence dominating second-moment estimates.
As an ablation, we compute <math id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> from <em id="A11.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">question+evidence</em> and report its impact.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">K.3 </span>Extended results (reference values)</h3>

<figure id="A11.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A11.T10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>: </span><span id="A11.T10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Extended error ratios on additional reasoning/RAG datasets and RAG representation ablations. Lower is better.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A11.T10.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A11.T10.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T10.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Dataset / Variant</td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Raw (mean)</td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Calibrated (mean)</td></tr>
<tr id="A11.T10.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T10.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">SVAMP (multi-step)</td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">2.15<math id="A11.T10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1.15<math id="A11.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A11.T10.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T10.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">NaturalQuestions (RAG)</td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">2.55<math id="A11.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.22<math id="A11.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A11.T10.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T10.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">HotpotQA (RAG, question-only <math id="A11.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">2.30<math id="A11.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.18<math id="A11.T10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A11.T10.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A11.T10.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">HotpotQA (RAG, question+evidence <math id="A11.T10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">2.55<math id="A11.T10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A11.T10.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">1.25<math id="A11.T10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A11.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis.</h5>

<div id="A11.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-step reasoning and RAG exhibit systematically larger raw error ratios than classification, consistent with higher demo sensitivity and additional prompt interactions.
Calibration reduces residual conservativeness in both families, typically bringing ratios close to <math id="A11.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times</annotation></semantics></math>.
For RAG, using question-only <math id="A11.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> tends to provide a cleaner second-moment signal; incorporating evidence can inflate the proxy and degrade tightness when evidence is noisy or heterogeneous.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A12" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix L </span>Direct Measurement of Distributional Stability (Definition 3.1)</h2>

<div id="A12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix directly measures the distributional stability criterion introduced in Definition 3.1, rather than relying on accuracy-based proxies. We explicitly quantify the variability of the model’s output distribution under independent resampling of demonstrations, and study how the resulting stability thresholds align with (i) empirical accuracy knee-points and (ii) our spectral proxy.</p>
</div>
<section id="A12.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.1 </span>Output distribution and divergence metric</h3>

<div id="A12.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed query <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and a sampled demonstration set <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, the prompted model induces a distribution over candidate answers,</p>
<table id="A12.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{S_{K}}(y\mid x_{q}),\qquad y\in\mathcal{Y}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{S_{K}}(y\mid x_{q}),\qquad y\in\mathcal{Y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For tasks with a closed answer set (e.g., multiple-choice), <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of options. For open-ended tasks, <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the union of the top-<math id="A12.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> decoded candidates across all seeds and <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> values, with <math id="A12.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=20</annotation></semantics></math>; probabilities are renormalized on this support.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To compare two output distributions, we use Jensen–Shannon divergence (JSD),</p>
<table id="A12.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{JSD}(p,q)=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{KL}(p\|m)+\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{KL}(q\|m),\qquad m=\tfrac{1}{2}(p+q)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>JSD</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{JSD}(p,q)=\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{KL}(p\|m)+\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{KL}(q\|m),\qquad m=\tfrac{1}{2}(p+q),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">measured in nats. JSD is symmetric, bounded, and empirically stable for finite-support distributions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.2 </span>Estimating stability probability</h3>

<div id="A12.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Definition 3.1 requires that, with high probability over independently sampled demonstration sets, the divergence between the resulting output distributions remains below a tolerance <math id="A12.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each query <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, demonstration size <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and tolerance <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, we estimate this probability by repeated resampling. Specifically, we draw <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=50</annotation></semantics></math> independent pairs of demonstration sets <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(S_{K}^{(r)},S_{K}^{\prime(r)})\}_{r=1}^{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(S_{K}^{(r)},S_{K}^{\prime(r)})\}_{r=1}^{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and compute</p>
<table id="A12.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{q}^{(r)}(K)=\mathrm{JSD}\!\left(p_{S_{K}^{(r)}}(\cdot\mid x_{q}),p_{S_{K}^{\prime(r)}}(\cdot\mid x_{q})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:2.007em;" width="2.007em"><mi>JSD</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{q}^{(r)}(K)=\mathrm{JSD}\!\left(p_{S_{K}^{(r)}}(\cdot\mid x_{q}),p_{S_{K}^{\prime(r)}}(\cdot\mid x_{q})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The per-query stability estimate is</p>
<table id="A12.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{q}(K;\tau)=\frac{1}{R}\sum_{r=1}^{R}\mathbf{1}\!\left[d_{q}^{(r)}(K)\leq\tau\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{q}(K;\tau)=\frac{1}{R}\sum_{r=1}^{R}\mathbf{1}\!\left[d_{q}^{(r)}(K)\leq\tau\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Aggregating over a dataset of <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=200</annotation></semantics></math> queries, we report the empirical stability probability</p>
<table id="A12.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Pi}(K;\tau)=\frac{1}{Q}\sum_{q=1}^{Q}\widehat{\pi}_{q}(K;\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Q</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Pi}(K;\tau)=\frac{1}{Q}\sum_{q=1}^{Q}\widehat{\pi}_{q}(K;\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For a fixed failure tolerance <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the direct stability threshold</p>
<table id="A12.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\star}_{\tau,\xi}=\min\left\{K:\widehat{\Pi}(K;\tau)\geq 1-\xi\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\star}_{\tau,\xi}=\min\left\{K:\widehat{\Pi}(K;\tau)\geq 1-\xi\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Unless stated otherwise, we use <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=0.10</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\{0.05,0.10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\{0.05,0.10\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.3 </span>Alignment with knee-points and spectral proxy</h3>

<div id="A12.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A12.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ L.3 Alignment with knee-points and spectral proxy ‣ Appendix L Direct Measurement of Distributional Stability (Definition 3.1) ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> compares the directly measured stability threshold <math id="A12.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\star}_{\tau,0.10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\star}_{\tau,0.10}</annotation></semantics></math> with the accuracy knee-point <math id="A12.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathrm{knee}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>knee</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathrm{knee}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the theory-driven spectral proxy prediction <math id="A12.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathrm{proxy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>proxy</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathrm{proxy}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Across all evaluated tasks, the three quantities are closely aligned, with discrepancies typically within a small constant.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A12.T11" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A12.T11.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A12.T11.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
