<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Direct measurement of distributional stability (Definition 3.1) using Jensen–Shannon divergence. <math id="A12.T11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\star}_{\tau,0.10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\star}_{\tau,0.10}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the smallest <math id="A12.T11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> such that the empirical stability probability exceeds <math id="A12.T11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math>. Results are compared with the accuracy knee-point and the spectral proxy prediction.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A12.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.4 </span>Stability probability and divergence quantiles</h3>

<div id="A12.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further characterize the stability transition, Table <a href="#A12.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ L.4 Stability probability and divergence quantiles ‣ Appendix L Direct Measurement of Distributional Stability (Definition 3.1) ‣ Stability of In-Context Learning: A Spectral Coverage Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> reports per-query quantiles of JSD aggregated over resampled demonstration pairs, together with the empirical stability probability <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Pi}(K;\tau=0.05)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Pi}(K;\tau=0.05)</annotation></semantics></math>.
As <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases, both the median and upper-tail divergences decrease sharply, and the <math id="A12.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90\%</annotation></semantics></math> stability criterion is reached near the predicted threshold.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A12.T12" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A12.T12.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A12.T12.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A12.T12.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A12.T12.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Task</span></td>
<td id="A12.T12.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A12.T12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A12.T12.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A12.T12.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Q50</span></td>
<td id="A12.T12.3.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A12.T12.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Q75</span></td>
<td id="A12.T12.3.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A12.T12.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Q90</span></td>
